<title>BELGIUM: LERNOUT LICENSES SPEECH TECHNOLOGY.</title>
<headline>LERNOUT LICENSES SPEECH TECHNOLOGY.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's Lernout &amp; Hauspie Speech Products NV said on Thursday it had licensed its text-to-speech and automatic speech recognition technology to U.S. communications software developer Medius Corporation.</p>
<p>Medius Corporation will use Lernout &amp; Hauspie's text-to-speech technology to allow travellers to call their personal computers and have electronic mail read to them over the phone.</p>
<p>The company says users will be able to retrieve voice mail and e-mail messages with one phone call.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
